<title>USA: FMR group cuts Hills Stores stake.</title>
<headline>FMR group cuts Hills Stores stake.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by FMR Corp, the parent of the investment adviser to Fidelity Funds, said Tuesday it reduced its stake in Hills Stores Co to 6.64 percent, from 9.03 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions include the sale of 244,377 shares between August 6 and 15 at prices ranging from $7.06 to $7.80 a share.</p>
<p>It said it now holds 676,837 common shares in Hills Stores.</p>
